---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY MAPPING (web → native)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  props:  metrics.alertsByType {severity:count} + metrics.alertTotal + alertPieData
            → one canonical [severity:count] map pushed by AlertsSectionSource;
              AlertsProjection.data() derives BOTH the severity rows AND the donut
              slices from it (DRY; web split into two props is the same data).
  shell:  <FadeIn delay={0.25}> + <GlassPanel space-y-6 p-6>
            → TSFadeIn(delay:0.25) + tokenized glass card (Color.TS.surface +
              TSRadius.lg + Color.TS.border stroke).
  header: <AlertTriangle text-neon-amber> + t('…alertsSection','Alerts') +
          alertTotal>0 ? <Badge variant=warning>{fmtInt}</Badge>
            → AlertsHeader: exclamationmark.triangle.fill (Color.TS.statusWarning)
              + panel title + AlertsCountBadge(total, .warning) shown only when >0
              + freshness chip.
  empty:  alertTotal===0 ? <EmptyState AlertTriangle "No alerts this week — …">
            → .empty phase → AlertsEmpty (ContentUnavailableView, checkmark.shield).
  list:   "Alerts by Severity" → Object.entries(alertsByType).map(row GlassPanel:
          critical=AlertCircle/STATUS_COLORS.critical, warning=AlertTriangle/
          STATUS_COLORS.warning, info=Info/CHART_COLORS[0]; capitalize label;
          Badge danger/warning/info {fmtInt(count)})
            → AlertsSeverityList + AlertsSeverityRow: AlertsPalette.symbol/.color per
              AlertSeverityKind (adaptive semantic tokens, not static hex — light/
              dark/high-contrast safe) + label(localize:) + AlertsCountBadge.
  pie:    "Alert Distribution" → <PieChart><Pie inner55 outer90 data=alertPieData>
          <Cell fill=entry.color/> <Tooltip ChartTooltip/> <Legend/>
            → AlertDistribution + AlertDonutChart: Chart{ SectorMark(innerRadius
              .ratio(0.62)) } per slice, AlertsPalette.color(for:kind), center total
              readout, tappable AlertDistributionLegend (swatch+label+count) that
              selects+highlights a slice and swaps the center to count + % share.
  fmt:    fmtInt(n) → AlertsFormat.count(n) (locale-aware grouped integer).
  cap:    severity.charAt(0).toUpperCase()+slice(1) → AlertsProjection.capitalizeFirst
          (unknown severities render the capitalized raw key; known → localized).
  i18n:   t('analytics.weeklyDigest.alertsSection|noAlerts|alertsBySeverity|
          alertDistribution', …) → AlertsStrings facade, table "AlertsSection".

STATES (every one renders — no hidden surface):
  loading  → AlertsLoading (TSSkeleton rows + donut; reduce-motion safe)
  content  → AlertsContent (responsive: lg 2-column HStack / compact VStack) =
             AlertsSeverityList + AlertDistribution
  empty    → AlertsEmpty (ContentUnavailableView, web "…noAlerts" message)
  error    → AlertsError (QueryError-equiv, Retry → model.refresh())
  stale    → freshness chip (Stale) + AlertsConnectivityBanner + ONE guarded auto-refresh
  offline  → freshness chip (Offline) + banner; keeps cached counts, no refetch
a11y: container summary (title + total + per-severity counts), per-row VoiceOver
  value, per-slice VoiceOver label/value, legend rows are buttons with
  isSelected trait, reduce-motion animation gate, Dynamic Type via system
  fonts/tokens.
telemetry: P1/S11 view.opened(surface:"AlertsSection") emitted once on appear.
binding: P1/S8 AlertsSectionSource seam (production impl over shared state holders);
  the view performs NO networking. Previews/tests drive InMemoryAlertsSectionSource.

